From: SKJ Wine <skj-tech@hotmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypt32: Fail CryptAcquireCertificatePrivateKey with CRYPT_ACQUIRE_ONLY_NCRYPT_KEY_FLAG.

Wine's crypt32 only ever returns legacy CAPI (HCRYPTPROV) handles. When a
caller passes CRYPT_ACQUIRE_ONLY_NCRYPT_KEY_FLAG it trusts the returned
handle to be an NCRYPT_KEY_HANDLE. .NET (Core) does exactly this in
CertificatePal.TryAcquireCngPrivateKey() and then calls NCryptGetProperty()
on the CAPI handle, which crashes with an AccessViolationException.

Failing the request makes .NET fall back to the CSP (CAPI) path, which
Wine supports. Seen with SteelSeries GG (SteelSeriesGGEZ.exe, .NET 8).
---
 dlls/crypt32/cert.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/crypt32/cert.c b/dlls/crypt32/cert.c
--- a/dlls/crypt32/cert.c
+++ b/dlls/crypt32/cert.c
@@ -1020,6 +1020,14 @@ BOOL WINAPI CryptAcquireCertificatePrivateKey(PCCERT_CONTEXT pCert,
     TRACE("(%p, %08lx, %p, %p, %p, %p)\n", pCert, dwFlags, pvReserved,
      phCryptProv, pdwKeySpec, pfCallerFreeProv);
 
+    if (dwFlags & CRYPT_ACQUIRE_ONLY_NCRYPT_KEY_FLAG)
+    {
+        /* we never hand out NCrypt key handles, don't pretend a CAPI one is */
+        FIXME("CRYPT_ACQUIRE_ONLY_NCRYPT_KEY_FLAG not supported, failing\n");
+        SetLastError(NTE_BAD_PROVIDER);
+        return FALSE;
+    }
+
     if (dwFlags & CRYPT_ACQUIRE_USE_PROV_INFO_FLAG)
     {
         DWORD size = 0;
